==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is an [[Eyes of Forced Unconscious Sleep (Enemy Base)|Eyes of Forced Unconscious Sleep]].
*2 [[Pigeon de Sable]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
*2 [[Zroco]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Demon Doge]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.
*1 [[Owlbrow]] spawns after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Enmu]] spawns as the boss.
**3 [[Zroco]]s spawn, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
**2 [[Zir Zeal]]s spawn after 1.33 seconds<sup>40f</sup>, delay 73.33~80 seconds<sup>2,200f~2,400f</sup>.
**1 [[Owlbrow]] spawns after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
**5 [[Pigeon de Sable]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
**1 [[Zang Roo]] spawns after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Zroco]]s spawn after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage features Zombie Enemies keeping frontline pressure while Enmu sits in the back and occasionally releases a heavy hit with a Freeze on your units. [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]] is a no-brainer here due to the Zombies, and can exploit Enmu's low attack rate to keep them busy. Speaking of their low attack rate, rushers and quick damage dealers will excel at getting hits on them. [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]], [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]], and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] are some of the stronger units filling this role. The Zombies can be dealt with using a mix of [[Zombie Killer|Zombie Killers]] and Crowd-Controllers. [[Gardener Cat (Rare Cat)|Weedwhacker Cat]] and [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]] are good options for this. Hold your ground until Enmu is dead and the stage is basically won. If you find yourself having trouble against the Owlbrow or Pigeon De Sable, you can bring [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] to get rid of them quickly, and they can also serve as a generalist rusher to sneak hits onto Enmu. Note that since the Enemy Base is animated, units with Surges or Explosions can tear it down even quicker

This stage can also be rushed with [[Talents|Talented]] Awakened Bahamut Cat for the timed rewards (at Lv.40+ with a Defense Up [[Cat Combo]]). Simply send out Maglev Cat (at least Lv.46 to K.O. the Zroco) to kill the Pigeon de Sable for Extra Money, then send out Bahamut. Awakened Bahamut Cat will ideally trigger the boss with his Explosions, baiting an attack from Enmu before quickly destroying the enemy base. The defense Cat Combo is necessary to tank a hit from Owlbrow.

